","def":"a mart","kjv":"merchandise.","count":1},"H4820":{"lemma":"מִרְמָה","xlit":"mirmâh","pron":"meer-maw'","from":"from H7411 (רָמָה) in the sense of deceiving;","def":"fraud","kjv":"craft, deceit(-ful, -fully), false, feigned, guile, subtilly, treachery.","count":39},"H4821":{"lemma":"מִרְמָה","xlit":"Mirmâh","pron":"meer-maw'","from":"the same as H4820 (מִרְמָה);","def":"Mirmah, an Israelite","kjv":"Mirma.","count":1},"H4822":{"lemma":"מְרֵמוֹת","xlit":"Mᵉrêmôwth","pron":"mer-ay-mohth'","from":"plural from H7311 (רוּם); heights;","def":"Meremoth, the name of two Israelites","kjv":"Meremoth.","count":6},"H4823":{"lemma":"מִרְמָס","xlit":"mirmâç","pron":"meer-mawce'","from":"from H7429 (רָמַס);","def":"abasement (the act or the thing)","kjv":"tread (down) -ing, (to be) trodden (down) under foot.","count":7},"H4824":{"lemma":"מֵרֹנֹתִי","xlit":"Mêrônôthîy","pron":"may-ro-no-thee'","from":"patrial from an unused noun;","def":"a Meronothite, or inhabitant of some (otherwise unknown) Meronoth.","kjv":"Meronothite.","count":2},"H4825":{"lemma":"מֶרֶס","xlit":"Mereç","pron":"meh'-res","from":"of foreign derivation;","def":"Meres, a Persian","kjv":"Meres.","count":1},"H4826":{"lemma":"מַרְסְנָא","xlit":"Marçᵉnâʼ","pron":"mar-sen-aw'","from":"of foreign derivation;","def":"Marsena, a Persian","kjv":"Marsena.","count":1},"H4827":{"lemma":"מֵרַע","xlit":"mêraʻ","pron":"may-rah'","from":"from H7489 (רָעַע);","def":"used as (abstract) noun, wickedness","kjv":"do mischief.","count":1},"H4828":{"lemma":"מֵרֵעַ","xlit":"mêrêaʻ","pron":"may-ray'-ah","from":"from H7462 (רָעָה) in the sense of companionship;","def":"a friend","kjv":"companion, friend.","count":7},"H4829":{"lemma":"מִרְעֶה","xlit":"mirʻeh","pron":"meer-eh'","from":"from H7462 (רָעָה) in the sense of feeding;","def":"pasture (the place or the act); also the haunt of wild animals","kjv":"feeding place, pasture.","count":13},"H4830":{"lemma":"מִרְעִית","xlit":"mirʻîyth","pron":"meer-eeth'","from":"from H7462 (רָעָה) 